AutoPrimeNet 2.0.2: macOS libcrypto stub + farm ECM "remaining worktodo" queue
=============================================================================

Local deployment patch for the farm (not submitted upstream).  Apply it on top of
the three patches in this directory:

  autoprimenet-2.0.2-prime95-report-only.patch
  autoprimenet-2.0.2-untrusted-fetch.patch
  autoprimenet-2.0.2-ecm-keep-open.patch

It contains two independent fixes:

1. macOS: Apple's /usr/lib/libcrypto.dylib is a stub.  dlopen()ing it aborts the
   process with "Python is loading libcrypto in an unsafe way" / SIGABRT.  Only
   accept a real OpenSSL library outside /usr/lib and /System; the optional AES
   helper is then simply disabled.  Needed to run AutoPrimeNet with the system
   python3 on macOS.

2. Farm: the ECM d=0 logic added by the ecm-keep-open patch looks for remaining
   curves in AutoPrimeNet's own worktodo file.  In a farm the program (mprime)
   owns the worktodo file and AutoPrimeNet only reports results, so its worktodo
   is empty and every result would still go out with d=1, closing the 50-curve
   assignment after the first curve.  With APN_ECM_REMAINING_WORKTODO pointing
   at mprime's worktodo, the remaining curves are counted from that file.
   Verified on 2026-11-19: one curve submitted while 49 were still queued ->
   request carried d=0, PrimeNet accepted the result and kept the assignment
   open; the first four test curves submitted with an empty queue carried d=1.

--- a/autoprimenet.py
+++ b/autoprimenet.py
@@ -809,6 +809,13 @@
 		break
 	else:
 		libcrypto = find_library("crypto") or find_library("eay32")
+		# Apple's /usr/lib/libcrypto.dylib is a stub: dlopen() aborts the process
+		# with "Python is loading libcrypto in an unsafe way" and SIGABRT, so only
+		# accept a real OpenSSL library outside the system directories (e.g.
+		# Homebrew's or python.org's).  The AES helper is optional, so leaving
+		# libcrypto unset is safe.
+		if libcrypto and (libcrypto.startswith("/usr/lib") or libcrypto.startswith("/System/")):
+			libcrypto = None
 else:
 	libcrypto = find_library("crypto") or find_library("eay32")
 
@@ -8091,6 +8098,12 @@
 		# last curve (or a found factor) closes it.  The stock code always sent
 		# d=1, which makes PrimeNet close the assignment after the first curve
 		# and turns all remaining curves into "invalid assignment key" results.
+		#
+		# The queue normally lives in AutoPrimeNet's own worktodo file.  When the
+		# program keeps it somewhere else (e.g. a farm where mprime owns the
+		# worktodo file and AutoPrimeNet only reports results), set
+		# APN_ECM_REMAINING_WORKTODO to that file and the remaining curves are
+		# counted from it, so d=0 still keeps the assignment open.
 		if result_type == PRIMENET_AR.ECM_FACTOR:
 			params["d"] = 1
 		else:
@@ -8097,15 +8110,29 @@
-			params["d"] = (
-				0
-				if any(
-					task.k == assignment.k
-					and task.b == assignment.b
-					and task.n == assignment.n
-					and task.c == assignment.c
-					for task in tasks
-					if isinstance(task, Assignment)
-				)
-				else 1
+			keep_open = any(
+				task.k == assignment.k
+				and task.b == assignment.b
+				and task.n == assignment.n
+				and task.c == assignment.c
+				for task in tasks
+				if isinstance(task, Assignment)
 			)
+			remaining_file = os.environ.get("APN_ECM_REMAINING_WORKTODO")
+			if not keep_open and remaining_file:
+				try:
+					with open(remaining_file, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as remaining:
+						for line in remaining:
+							match = ECM_RE.match(line.strip())
+							if (
+								match
+								and int(match.group(3)) == assignment.k
+								and int(match.group(4)) == assignment.b
+								and int(match.group(5)) == assignment.n
+								and int(match.group(6)) == assignment.c
+							):
+								keep_open = True
+								break
+				except OSError:
+					pass
+			params["d"] = 0 if keep_open else 1
 		params.update((("A", assignment.k), ("b", assignment.b), ("c", assignment.c)))
 		params["CR"] = ar["curves"]
 		params["B1"] = ar["b1"]
